(6, 'Product of Array Except Self', 'product-of-array-except-self', 'Medium', 'Arrays & Hashing', '["Arrays", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '47.6%', 686, 38, '<p>Given an integer array nums, return an array answer such that answer[i] is equal to the product of all the elements of nums except nums[i].</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> nums=[1,2,3,4]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [24,12,8,6]</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "nums=[1,2,3,4]"}, "expected": "[24,12,8,6]"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Product of Array Except Self utilizes Arrays & Hashing techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
