(9, 'First Missing Positive', 'first-missing-positive', 'Hard', 'Arrays & Hashing', '["Arrays", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '68.0%', 779, 47, '<p>Given an unsorted integer array nums. Return the smallest positive integer that is not present in nums.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> nums=[1,2,0]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 3</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "nums=[1,2,0]"}, "expected": "3"}, {"input_params": {"input": "nums=[3,4,-1,1]"}, "expected": "2"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for First Missing Positive utilizes Arrays & Hashing techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
(10, 'Valid Palindrome', 'valid-palindrome', 'Easy', 'Two Pointers', '["Two", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '40.1%', 810, 50, '<p>A phrase is a palindrome if, after converting all uppercase letters into lowercase letters and removing all non-alphanumeric characters, it reads the same forward and backward.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> s=\'A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\'\n<strong>Output:</strong> true</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "s=\'A man, a plan, a canal: Panama\'"}, "expected": "true"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Valid Palindrome utilizes Two Pointers techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
(11, 'Two Sum II - Input Array Is Sorted', 'two-sum-ii-input-array-is-sorted', 'Medium', 'Two Pointers', '["Two", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '47.2%', 841, 53, '<p>Given a 1-indexed array of integers numbers that is already sorted in non-decreasing order, find two numbers such that they add up to a specific target number.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> numbers=[2,7,11,15], target=9\n<strong>Output:</strong> [1,2]</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "numbers=[2,7,11,15], target=9"}, "expected": "[1,2]"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Two Sum II - Input Array Is Sorted utilizes Two Pointers techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
(12, '3Sum', '3sum', 'Medium', 'Two Pointers', '["Two", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '54.3%', 872, 56, '<p>Given an integer array nums, return all the triplets [nums[i], nums[j], nums[k]] such that i != j, i != k, and j != k, and nums[i] + nums[j] + nums[k] == 0.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> nums=[-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]]</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "nums=[-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]"}, "expected": "[[-1,-1,2],[-1,0,1]]"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for 3Sum utilizes Two Pointers techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
(13, 'Container With Most Water', 'container-with-most-water', 'Medium', 'Two Pointers', '["Two", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '61.4%', 903, 59, '<p>Find two lines that together with the x-axis form a container, such that the container contains the most water.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> height=[1,8,6,2,5,4,8,3,7]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 49</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "height=[1,8,6,2,5,4,8,3,7]"}, "expected": "49"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Container With Most Water utilizes Two Pointers techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
(14, 'Trapping Rain Water', 'trapping-rain-water', 'Hard', 'Two Pointers', '["Two", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '68.5%', 934, 62, '<p>Given n non-negative integers representing an elevation map where the width of each bar is 1, compute how much water it can trap after raining.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> height=[0,1,0,2,1,0,1,3,2,1,2,1]\n<strong>Output:</strong> 6</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "height=[0,1,0,2,1,0,1,3,2,1,2,1]"}, "expected": "6"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Trapping Rain Water utilizes Two Pointers techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
