(28, 'Search a 2D Matrix', 'search-a-2d-matrix', 'Medium', 'Binary Search', '["Binary", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '61.1%', 1368, 104, '<p>Write an efficient algorithm that searches for a value target in an m x n integer matrix.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> matrix=[[1,3,5,7],[10,11,16,20],[23,30,34,60]], target=3\n<strong>Output:</strong> true</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "matrix=[[1,3,5,7],[10,11,16,20],[23,30,34,60]], target=3"}, "expected": "true"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Search a 2D Matrix utilizes Binary Search techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
