(49, 'Kth Smallest Element in a BST', 'kth-smallest-element-in-a-bst', 'Medium', 'Trees', '["Trees", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '68.4%', 2019, 167, '<p>Given the root of a binary search tree, and an integer k, return the kth smallest value in the tree.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> root=[3,1,4,null,2], k=1\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "root=[3,1,4,null,2], k=1"}, "expected": "1"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Kth Smallest Element in a BST utilizes Trees techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
(50, 'Construct Binary Tree from Preorder and Inorder Traversal', 'construct-binary-tree-from-preorder-and-inorder-traversal', 'Medium', 'Trees', '["Trees", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '40.5%', 2050, 20, '<p>Given two integer arrays preorder and inorder, construct and return the binary tree.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> preorder=[3,9,20,15,7], inorder=[9,3,15,20,7]\n<strong>Output:</strong> [3,9,20,null,null,15,7]</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "preorder=[3,9,20,15,7], inorder=[9,3,15,20,7]"}, "expected": "[3,9,20,null,null,15,7]"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Construct Binary Tree from Preorder and Inorder Traversal utilizes Trees techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32');
