(97, 'Reverse Integer', 'reverse-integer', 'Medium', 'Bit Manipulation & Math', '["Bit", "Algorithm", "Coding"]', '54.7%', 3507, 161, '<p>Given a signed 32-bit integer x, return x with its digits reversed. If reversing x causes the value to go outside the signed 32-bit integer range, then return 0.</p>\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> x=123\n<strong>Output:</strong> 321</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= input.length <= 10^5", "Values are within standard 32-bit integer limits.", "Optimized time complexity expected (O(N) or O(N log N))."]', '["Consider the edge cases such as empty input or single element.", "Think about using a suitable data structure for fast lookup."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solve(self, input_data):\\n        # Write your optimal solution here\\n        pass\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {any} inputData\\n * @return {any}\\n */\\nfunction solve(inputData) {\\n    // Write your optimal solution here\\n}\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solve(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        // Optimal C++ solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solve(int[] nums) {\\n        // Optimal Java solution\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"input": "x=123"}, "expected": "321"}, {"input_params": {"input": "x=-123"}, "expected": "-321"}]', '[{"input_params": {"input": "EdgeCase_1"}, "expected": "OptimalResult"}]', 'Standard approach for Reverse Integer utilizes Bit Manipulation & Math techniques with optimal time and space complexity.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
(100, 'Matrix Diagonal Sum', 'matrix-diagonal-sum', 'Easy', 'Arrays & Hashing', '["Arrays", "Competitive Programming", "Placement Ready"]', '55.1%', 2100, 30, '<p>You are given a problem statement focusing on <strong>Arrays & Hashing</strong> algorithms and data structures.</p>\n<p>Solve <strong>Matrix Diagonal Sum</strong> with optimal time and space complexity constraints.</p>\n<p>Analyze edge cases, handle constraints, and return the exact answer satisfying standard automated judge assertions.</p>\n\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> data = [1, 2, 4, 8], threshold = 3\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Optimal combination satisfies all constraints within the Arrays & Hashing domain.</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= n <= 10^5", "-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9", "Time Complexity: O(N log N) or O(N)", "Space Complexity: O(1) or O(N)"]', '["Consider how Arrays & Hashing properties simplify this problem.", "Draw the decision tree or state transitions on paper."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solveProblem(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:\\n        # Implement optimal Arrays & Hashing algorithm\\n        return len(nums)\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {number[]} nums\\n * @return {number}\\n */\\nvar solveProblem = function(nums) {\\n    // Implement optimal Arrays & Hashing algorithm\\n    return nums.length;\\n};\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solveProblem(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        return nums.size();\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solveProblem(int[] nums) {\\n        return nums.length;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"nums": [1, 2, 4, 8], "threshold": 3}, "expected": "4"}, {"input_params": {"nums": [10, 20, 30], "threshold": 5}, "expected": "3"}]', '[{"input_params": {"nums": [5, 15, 25, 35, 45], "threshold": 2}, "expected": "5"}]', 'This problem is best solved using Arrays & Hashing patterns with strict linear or logarithmic time boundaries.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
