(303, 'Fibonacci Number (Track 2)', 'fibonacci-number-track-2', 'Easy', '1-D DP', '["1-D", "Competitive Programming", "Placement Ready"]', '38.6%', 957, 85, '<p>You are given a problem statement focusing on <strong>1-D DP</strong> algorithms and data structures.</p>\n<p>Solve <strong>Fibonacci Number (Track 2)</strong> with optimal time and space complexity constraints.</p>\n<p>Analyze edge cases, handle constraints, and return the exact answer satisfying standard automated judge assertions.</p>\n\n<div class="problem-example-card">\n  <h4>Example 1:</h4>\n  <pre><code><strong>Input:</strong> data = [1, 2, 4, 8], threshold = 3\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Optimal combination satisfies all constraints within the 1-D DP domain.</code></pre>\n</div>', '["1 <= n <= 10^5", "-10^9 <= nums[i] <= 10^9", "Time Complexity: O(N log N) or O(N)", "Space Complexity: O(1) or O(N)"]', '["Consider how 1-D DP properties simplify this problem.", "Draw the decision tree or state transitions on paper."]', '{"python3": "class Solution:\\n    def solveProblem(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:\\n        # Implement optimal 1-D DP algorithm\\n        return len(nums)\\n", "javascript": "/**\\n * @param {number[]} nums\\n * @return {number}\\n */\\nvar solveProblem = function(nums) {\\n    // Implement optimal 1-D DP algorithm\\n    return nums.length;\\n};\\n", "cpp": "class Solution {\\npublic:\\n    int solveProblem(vector<int>& nums) {\\n        return nums.size();\\n    }\\n};\\n", "java": "class Solution {\\n    public int solveProblem(int[] nums) {\\n        return nums.length;\\n    }\\n}\\n"}', '[{"input_params": {"nums": [1, 2, 4, 8], "threshold": 3}, "expected": "4"}, {"input_params": {"nums": [10, 20, 30], "threshold": 5}, "expected": "3"}]', '[{"input_params": {"nums": [5, 15, 25, 35, 45], "threshold": 2}, "expected": "5"}]', 'This problem is best solved using 1-D DP patterns with strict linear or logarithmic time boundaries.', '2026-11-07 05:50:32'),
